WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.589
Now, you used to see a lot of scientific
counsel within government. It was a

00:00:04.589 --> 00:00:09.389
common thing during most of my lifespan:
Offices of Technology Assessment and so

00:00:09.389 --> 00:00:13.679
forth. A lot of these guys cluttering up
the scene in government. They are a dying

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:19.740
breed. Because fundamentalists and
oligarchs both despise science. They

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:22.830
don't want it to have anything to do with them. Now

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:29.369
in this ancient standard of futurism, the
gold standard is Vannevar Bush, from the

00:00:29.369 --> 00:00:34.320
1940s, who was one of the inventors of
the atomic bomb. A master engineer of the

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.219
Manhattan Project. He was also the father
of the American National Science

00:00:38.219 --> 00:00:42.360
Foundation, because he wrote the
extremely important futurist text,

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:48.450
Science: The Endless Frontier. That screed
is probably the greatest work of

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:53.550
futurism ever put onto paper with a
typewriter. It's really an impressive

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:59.250
governmental document. And, you know, aimed at the head of state. So there's

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:04.290
still a problem with this. It's like: why
isn't science as respected as it was? And

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:08.930
I think the problem there is cultural. Because Americans, and especially

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:15.840
Californians, have a severe moral problem
with the idea that frontiers end. But

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:20.520
they're not endless. In fact, that gold
rushes just get old and die ugly;

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:23.490
they're not always young and pretty and
beautiful and glamorous and

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:28.229
forward-looking. They get old and cranky
and weird and obsessed

00:01:28.229 --> 00:01:32.790
with themselves. And it kind of like
moved from, you know,

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:38.490
from savagery to barbarism without
civilization ever occurring. Savagery

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:43.320
barbarism, the decadence without without
a civilization, is a typical frontier

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.369
development. So you know to think that
the science is an endless frontier is

00:01:47.369 --> 00:01:52.700
actually a bad paradigm, especially for a
futurist or a scientist. For instance,

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:57.580
paleontology is an important science,
which is about things that ended a long

00:01:57.580 --> 00:02:02.060
time ago. And they just ended. They're not
gone; they're not gonna revive. You're not

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:07.380
gonna improve the trilobites, right?
But it's important to understand

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:11.300
what's going on in geologic time whether
there's anything to do with it or not.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:15.299
And there are also many areas of
scientific investigation that are not

00:02:15.299 --> 00:02:19.500
endless frontiers, they're dead ends. I mean
they're cul-de-sacs. They have to be

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:26.040
abandoned, such as phlogiston, you know? Or
the luminiferous ether, or spontaneous

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.720
generation, or even some aspects of
Newtonian physics.

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.250
They're not up to speed, and, you know, you
have to let those go. Scientific truth is

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:40.530
provisional; it's not permanent and
eternal. And science as a human

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:45.409
enterprise, I mean the actual business of
science, and how scientists are

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:49.859
recruited, promoted, how they quote one
another, that's a very time-bound, very

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:55.950
social kind of situation that changes
quite a lot as time as time goes on. So

00:02:55.950 --> 00:03:00.359
if you think that atomic physics, or
maybe, the truth of atomic physics, the

00:03:00.359 --> 00:03:06.389
scientific truth of atomic physics, is
somehow an eternal thing, then you have

00:03:06.389 --> 00:03:11.340
to go all-out for nuclear power, or giant
gadgets like the superconducting

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:17.010
supercollider, which is unwise. That ambition is going to end in tears.

00:03:17.010 --> 00:03:22.410
If you ask the government for 11 billion
dollars for a superb scientific

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:27.599
instrument that is not going to work
—it can't be built—

00:03:27.599 --> 00:03:32.280
that is bad politics. It's poor
statesmanship. You're a scientific

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:38.430
futurist, but you gave bad advice. So if
you're a scientific futurist and you're

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.599
in the government pace layer, you can't
simply say to them, "I have some

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:48.720
inconvenient truth here, look at this
math." It won't work. You have to say, "I

00:03:48.720 --> 00:03:52.949
have some inconvenient truth here, and I
can use it to win World War II with a

00:03:52.949 --> 00:04:00.569
secret super weapon." That was the Vannevar
Bush method and that's what life

00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:04.169
is like in the government pace layer
when things are really cracking right

00:04:04.169 --> 00:04:06.590
along.

